diate counter-attacks that would flip it back (unlike moves to B4 or C5), securing a net material gain even if the opponent retakes C4.\nAnswer: (C,3) -> (D,3)\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: The move (C,3) -> (D,3) is a safe expansion that captures an opponent piece.\nReason: By cloning to D3, I increase my piece count and capture the opponent's piece at C4. The new piece at D3 is strategically placed to resist immediate counter-attacks that would flip it back (unlike moves to B4 or C5 which are susceptible to the strong enemy cluster at B6/A6), securing a net material gain even if the opponent subsequently retakes C4.\nAnswer: (C,3) -> (D,3)"}
